Description: Auto DJ fixes found on the hardware: fill without loading, early outros, GUI stalls
 - Random tracks for the queue (patch 0022: 8 candidates placed by key and
   tempo) are read from the database (ids, files, bpm, key_id) instead of
   being loaded as tracks; the queue's key and tempo too. This runs in the
   GUI thread at every transition: with a large library, loading 8 + 10
   tracks stalled it for about half a second.
 - An outro that ends in the first tenth of a track is ignored (as not
   set): a file the decoder could not read is analysed as silence, with
   intro, outro and last sound all at 0, and Auto DJ left such a track a
   few seconds after it started. Test FullIntroOutro_OutroAtStartIgnored.
 - DECKSMITHOS_GUI_STALL_MS: a warning "GUI thread stalled for N ms" when a
   20 ms timer of the GUI thread comes later than that, to find what stalls
   the waveforms on the hardware.
Author: DecksmithOS
Forwarded: no
Last-Update: 2026-11-24
